# TOKEN ECONOMY (Layer 0 — full)

Always-on stub: @.cursor/rules/token-economy-stub.mdc (§0.5.1 · §0.9 · handoff). **Read this file** on role command and before PLAN/DECOMPOSE/VAN artifact writes (§0.0).

Cross-cutting. Restricts **format**, not **content**. Quality (TDD, review, edge cases) > economy when conflict.

## 0.0 SUSPENSION GUARD — PLAN / gap-plan / architecture / **DECOMPOSE** artifacts (AUTHORITATIVE)

**Trigger (any of):**
- Role command: `BACK PLAN`, `FRONT PLAN`, `INTEG PLAN`, `PM PLAN`, `* SECURITY PLAN`, `* REFACTOR PLAN`, or any `* PLAN`
- Role command: `BACK DECOMPOSE`, `FRONT DECOMPOSE`, `INTEG DECOMPOSE` (and SECURITY/REFACTOR DECOMPOSE when writing step shards)
- Role command brownfield: `BACK VAN`, `FRONT VAN`, `INTEG VAN` when writing `memory-bank/architecture/**`
- Writing/updating: `memory-bank/**/plan-*.md`, `memory-bank/**/plan/decompose-*/**`, `memory-bank/integration/gap/**/gap-*.md`, gap closing plans `plan-BACK-GAP-*` / `plan-FRONT-GAP-*`, `memory-bank/**/security/plan/plan-*.md`, `memory-bank/**/refactor/plan/plan-*.md`, или `memory-bank/architecture/**`

### FORBIDDEN while guard is active (plan/gap/architecture/**decompose** OUTPUT)

- Apply §0.2 telegraph brevity to the plan/gap/**architecture**/`decompose-*/` file
- Cap size (~200 lines, «keep short», «оглавление достаточно», «мало шагов»)
- Compress Element/API registry / omit routes or UI elements / omit mermaid diagrams for length
- Compress DECOMPOSE: skip AC/FR/NFR/stages coverage, merge stages into infra-only sNN, refuse extra sNN «ради токенов»
- Treat chat «brief» as a reason to shorten `plan-*.md` / architecture / `decompose-*/**`
- Confuse lean **LOAD** (§0.3, §0.5.1) with lean **WRITE** of the plan/map/decompose

### REQUIRED

- Plan/gap/**architecture**/`decompose-*/index.md`+`sNN|eNN-*.yaml`: **maximally detailed, exhaustive, comprehensive** — no line/size/brevity limits on intent/coverage (DECOMPOSE still lean = no full code bodies in shards)
- Chat with user MAY stay brief (1–3 sentences summary); **artifact must not**
- Research/audit PLAN input with ≥2 cut criteria → **N epics** + roadmap (@.cursor/rules/shared/workflow-plan-multi-epic.mdc); one mega-plan that truncates = FAIL

### SUSPENDED for plan/gap/architecture/decompose artifact only

§0.2 · §0.5 size cap · §0.6 chunked execution · §0.12 single-pass economy · §0.15 session/chat economy **as applied to writing the plan/map/decompose file**

### RETAINED

§0.9 approval · §0.13 roles · §0.14 model routing · §0.10 session start / FINISH · lean **read** of unrelated shards (still don't dump whole memory-bank into context — but **do** inventory everything the PLAN / DECOMPOSE / brownfield VAN workflow requires)

This section **supersedes** every conflicting brevity rule. Workflow PLAN / DECOMPOSE / brownfield VAN files must restate it; if ignored → FAIL.

## 0.0.1 Load ≠ Write (Claude Code / Cursor)

| | Economy applies? | Notes |
|--|------------------|-------|
| **Which files you READ** | YES lean | `load_now`, ONE shard for IMPLEMENT; PLAN may inventory all required portal implement + routes |
| **How much of an allowed file you READ** | **NO line-cap** | Skills / `.cursor/rules` / code / step shard — **full file**. FORBIDDEN: `read … limit:200` «из-за §0.5» |
| **What you WRITE** to `plan-*.md` / `gap-*.md` / `architecture/**` / `decompose-*/**` | **NO lean** | §0.0 — full detail (DECOMPOSE: coverage+steps; still no code bodies in sNN) |
| **What you WRITE** to other `memory-bank/**` non-plan docs | YES §0.5 | max ~200 lines **on write/split** — not a read tool limit |
| **Chat reply to user** | YES brief OK | Do not mirror chat brevity into the plan/map/decompose file |

**Anti-pattern:** «Token economy → shorten plan/architecture/decompose» / «Token economy → read only 200 lines of SKILL.md».
**Correct:** lean **which** files to load; full **content** of those files; §0.5 caps **write size** of non-plan docs only.

